Accepted true; first parse nodes 7; reconstructed without another CYK run.
\image(figures/cyk_triangle.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Cells are half-open byte spans. The bottom row contains terminal facts; each higher row has one fewer, longer span. Empty cells are shown explicitly rather than omitted from the data.)
\alttext(A ten-cell triangle has A, A, B, B in its bottom row; empty, S, empty above; empty, C next; and a green S in the full-span top cell.)

A terminal leaf covers one byte. Every other recovered node has two nonempty
children that partition its span. A full binary tree with n leaves has n−1
internal nodes, hence 2n−1 total nodes: counting edges gives 2I=I+n−1 and
I=n−1. Native reconstruction returns exactly that many nodes in preorder,
using an explicit task stack to avoid recursion depth. It checks the visited
local witness structure and root consistency. Since a result does not retain
the original grammar, those checks do not certify arbitrary public edits
against that grammar. A cell accessor similarly validates bounds, vector
length and the selected coordinates, and returns a borrowed const reference
whose lifetime ends on owner mutation or destruction.

> Count geometry separately from successful work and ambiguity

Let m be the number of distinct nonterminal ids, including the start, and r
the number of raw binary productions. The number of positive-length cells Q
and split points K are

\[
Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^n(n-\ell+1)=\frac{n(n+1)}2,\qquad
K=\sum_{\ell=2}^n(n-\ell+1)(\ell-1)=\frac{n(n-1)(n+1)}6.
\]
\alttext(The triangular chart has n times n plus one divided by two cells. Trying every positive split over all cells gives n minus one times n times n plus one divided by six.)

The last identity also counts choices of three boundaries from n+1 boundary
positions. Dense membership storage has Qm slots. In the worst case each
split tests r rules, so Kr bounds binary-rule candidates. The kernel still
visits all K splits when children are empty; it skips the rule loop at those
splits. Actual rule tests can thus be far below Kr. These are operation
counts, not elapsed time or measurements of allocator/cache cost.

Use the ambiguous grammar S→SS | a. Every nonempty all-a substring derives S,
so every split reaches the binary rule. The exact counts are Q memberships,
K actual binary tests and K matching-rule events. For aaaa there are five
binary tree shapes: the Catalan recurrence C_j=Σ_{i=0}^{j−1}C_i C_{j−1−i},
C_0=1 gives C_1=1, C_2=2, C_3=5. A boolean chart stores one membership per
span, and the first-witness policy chooses split one, then proceeds rightward.
Neither a single recovered tree nor the count of matching-rule events counts
the full parses. Duplicating an identical grammar rule changes candidate/event
counts while leaving the language and distinct chart memberships unchanged.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cyk_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <climits>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::CNFGrammar g;g.unary['a']={0};g.binary={{0,0,0}};
  std::vector<double> sizes,cells,splits;
  std::print("| bytes | potential state slots | actual memberships | split points | actual rule tests | first parse nodes |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int n:{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128}) {
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(g,std::string(n,'a'));const auto p=dm::algorithms::cyk_first_parse(a);
    if(!a.accepted || a.work.new_states!=a.shape.cells || a.work.binary_rule_tests!=a.shape.splits || p.size()!=static_cast<std::size_t>(2*n-1)) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,a.shape.state_slots,a.work.new_states,a.work.split_points,a.work.binary_rule_tests,p.size());
    sizes.push_back(n);cells.push_back(a.work.new_states);splits.push_back(a.work.binary_rule_tests);
  }
  auto storage=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  storage.line(sizes,cells,"memberships",{37,99,235},2).points(sizes,cells,"",{37,99,235},4)
         .title("Quadratic chart memberships").x_label("input bytes n").y_label("distinct span memberships")
         .x_limits(0,135).y_limits(0,10500).size(540,480);
  auto work=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  work.line(sizes,splits,"binary tests",{220,38,38},2).points(sizes,splits,"",{220,38,38},4)
      .title("Cubic candidate tests for one rule").x_label("input bytes n").y_label("actual binary-rule tests")
      .x_limits(0,135).y_limits(0,440000).size(540,480);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(storage).add(work).size(1130,540)
    .title("S -> SS or a: every substring and every split succeeds").save_svg("build/cyk_work.svg");
  const auto first=dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(g,"aaaa");g.binary.push_back({0,0,0});const auto duplicate=dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(g,"aaaa");
  std::print("\nAmbiguous aaaa: one rule gives {} memberships, {} matching events and one {}-node returned parse. Duplicating the rule gives {} memberships and {} matching events.\n",first.work.new_states,first.work.matching_rules,dm::algorithms::cyk_first_parse(first).size(),duplicate.work.new_states,duplicate.work.matching_rules);
  int rejections=0;
  try {dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(g,"aaaa",9,0);} catch(const std::length_error&) {++rejections;}
  try {dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(g,"bbbb",0,19);} catch(const std::length_error&) {++rejections;}
  try {dm::algorithms::cyk_first_parse(first,6);} catch(const std::length_error&) {++rejections;}
  if(rejections!=3) return 1;
  const auto no_tokens=dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(g,"bbbb",0,0);
  dm::algorithms::CNFGrammar bytes;bytes.start=INT_MIN;bytes.unary['\0']={INT_MIN};const auto nul=dm::algorithms::cyk_analyze(bytes,std::string(1,'\0'));
  if(!nul.accepted || nul.nonterminals.size()!=1) return 1;
  std::print("Complete potential/node caps: {} expected rejections. With budgets disabled, bbbb visits {} splits and tests {} binary rules.\n",rejections,no_tokens.work.split_points,no_tokens.work.binary_rule_tests);
  std::print("Single NUL byte with INT_MIN start: accepted {}; byte length {}; compressed nonterminals {}.\n",nul.accepted,nul.input.size(),nul.nonterminals.size());
}
